<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<article article-type="research-article" xml:lang="en">
  <front>
    <journal-meta>
      <journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Fixture Bio Lett</journal-id>
      <issn pub-type="epub">1111-1111</issn>
    </journal-meta>
    <article-meta>
      <article-id pub-id-type="pmcid">PMCFIXTURE002</article-id>
      <title-group>
        <article-title>A low-quality fixture paper with sparse reporting</article-title>
      </title-group>
      <pub-date pub-type="epub"><year>2015</year></pub-date>
      <abstract><p>We investigated a treatment. Results were significant (p &lt; .05).</p></abstract>
    </article-meta>
  </front>
  <body>
    <sec>
      <title>Methods</title>
      <p>We recruited participants and gave them a drug. The data were analysed with Excel. No other
         details were recorded in this fixture low-quality paper. No sample size calculation was
         performed and we did not check assumptions.</p>
    </sec>
    <sec>
      <title>Results</title>
      <p>The treatment group did better than control (p &lt; .05). Some differences were seen. No
         effect sizes, confidence intervals, degrees of freedom, or exact test statistics are reported.
         No software version is given. No data availability statement is included.</p>
    </sec>
    <sec>
      <title>Discussion</title>
      <p>We conclude the treatment works.</p>
    </sec>
  </body>
</article>
